cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SUYA in your research, please cite it using the metadata in this file."
type: software
title: "SUYA: Antarctic ocean temperature, salinity and air temperature monitor"
abstract: >-
  SUYA is a desktop program that continuously collects Antarctic sea surface and
  subsurface temperature, salinity and coastal air temperature from public
  scientific APIs (NOAA METAR, Open-Meteo, NOAA OISST and MUR, SMOS and SMAP
  salinity, HYCOM ESPC-D-V02, Argo floats, GOSUD, World Ocean Atlas 2023 and the
  Windy Point Forecast API), stores every value with its provenance in SQLite and
  monthly Excel workbooks, and shows the data on a south-polar stereographic map
  with per-location profiles and time series. The interface is available in
  Korean and English.
